 "title": "Sync Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: a snarling, aggressive bass that rips at the start of each note, for industrial and EBM: hard sync in the low end.\n\nHow it's built: two oscillators an octave down; the second is synced to the first (SYNC), so it keeps the first's pitch while an envelope into its FM sweeps its tone: the rip. A filter takes off the fizz; a little Drive. One voice.\n\nPlay: short, punchy notes and riffs.\n\nTweak: the sweep envelope's DECAY, the second oscillator's FM and TUNE, the filter's CUTOFF.",
